{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/46642-need-help-conceptualizing-an-idea-for-a-conspiracy-the-incarnates","id":46642,"title":"Need help conceptualizing an idea for a Conspiracy: The Incarnates","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-01-10T18:18:19-08:00","id":46642,"title":"Need help conceptualizing an idea for a Conspiracy: The Incarnates","content":"An idea for a PC group popped into my head the other night, but I'm struggling to refine it into a workable state. Care to help me chop this up the right way?<br /> <br /> I'm seeing a group of modern Hunters (Tier 2 in numbers, but perhaps Tier 3 in mojo) who are (I can't decide which of these) descended from Hunters in the past or were those Hunters in a previous life. Their Endowment is about tapping that knowledge (I can definitely see a 'swap your ratings in two skills for one scene' ability) in order to better hunt monsters, at the risk of suffering uncontrollable personality/memory bleedover. I'm having a hard time getting at much beyond that, but I feel like this is a good idea.<br /> <br /> Should they be an organization at a specific point in time that are now coming back together via their descendants, or just people who share this odd ability to recall the skills of past lives and put them to work fighting supernaturals? I feel like I'm missing the meat of my own idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-10T19:32:38-08:00","id":46682,"title":"","content":"I can definitely accept this happening to people, but it begs the question of what prompts them to organize, the how, etc. What stops them from being the odd-member-out at other conspiracy/compact parties? Is there a common element to their dreams or visions that draw them together? What element ties it all together?<br /> <br /> If I may make a suggestion, they might all descend from the same group of people from a specific battle or place, where the thing that occurred that's caused them to reverberate through their progeny.<br /> <br /> At the risk of hitting the low hanging frruit, this reminds me of Assassin's Creed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-11T02:56:50-08:00","id":46815,"title":"","content":"Take a step back and ask yourselves a few simple questions:<br /> <br /> 1) What is the core theme of this group?<br /> 2) Why are these people all working together.<br /> 3) What is their goal? Why do they hunt monsters, or do they hunt something else like relics from their past lives?<br /> <br /> My general advice for Hunter homebrew is to see if you can come up with an interesting and playable (or fightable if you're mostly thinking about antagonists) group without any Endowment or mechanical tricks at all. If you can do that then you know you've got a good group, and the Endowment exists to enhance what's cool about them rather than be the coolness itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-11T09:43:30-08:00","id":46946,"title":"","content":"I would offer a counter opinion to Kings Raven, I feel it's perfectly acceptable to start from a mechanic and design theme around it. <br /> You can have a neat mechanical idea, and then work around it to incorporate story ideas to support it, and create a fully fleshed out group.<br /> <br /> So, here's some 'off the top of my head' stuff.<br /> <br /> <b>The Incarnates</b><br /> The soul is eternal. What happens to it after death, even the Archmagi cannot say for certain, even in the furthest depths of the underworld, Sin-Eaters know souls still travel onwards past the end. Where do they go? What do they do? We just don't know. But we do know one thing. Sometimes, under very specific circumstances, they can be reborn. When the order of the universe is upset enough, when things go far enough outside what is Natural, souls affected can become tied to the world not just as ghosts, but reborn over and over again into flesh, as new people.<br /> <br /> We are such souls, we are those lives afflicted by the supernatural, bound to the world, Incarnate in flesh.<br /> <br /> <br /> Incarnates are, like the Lucifuge, not so much a group you join, but one you are born into. Once you were a normal mortal, living a normal life, when something supernatural interfered. Maybe you died that day, or maybe you survived THAT encounter and became a hunter. But eventually, you died at the hands of a supernatural monster, and your life ended before you fulfilled your true purpose. You can't pass on, possibly you never will. Instead, with each death you are born again as a child somewhere in the world. And, if the Incarnate find you, they can help you remember who you were.<br /> <br /> The Incarnate are an organization of hunters who have suffered one of the most personal wrongs possible at the hands of some supernatural threat. They died. Possibly (probably) more than once. Their hatred of the supernatural is inborn, a burning legacy from lives past. So too is their weapon for fighting such threats.<br /> <br /> <b>Endowment: Pastlife (* - *****)</b><br /> When you create an Incarnate, during the skill selection step, in addition to your current character skills, you need to make a second set of skills (cut out just the skill section from another character sheet) for your past life. Pick a time period for your past life and substitute out skills that don't make sense for ones appropriate to that time period, E.G. Firearms becomes Archery, Drive becomes Ride, etc. Also remember that Medicine, academics, politics, and science from a 17th century view point aren't going to mean the same thing (but that doesn't mean they aren't useful). Distribute 13/9/5 between your pastlife skills, and pick 4 specialties. You may purchase more skills and specialties for your pastlife at half the normal ExP cost rounded up (this represents getting more intune with your pastlife, not your pastlife actually improving)<br /> During a scene, you may spend a willpower point to sub out one of your skills for the appropriate skill from your past life (trade your Weaponry for your pastlife's Weaponry, or trade your Drive for your pastlife's Ride, Etc.) along with any attendant Specialties (trade your Crafts 1 knitting for your pastlive's Crafts 5 Blacksmithing Swordsmithing). At 3 dots you may sub out Two skills for the Scene, and at 5 dots you may sub out 3 skills, each skill takes a willpower to sub out. At the end of the Scene, Roll your REGULAR skill + your PASTLIFE'S skill + 1 per specialty, Minus your Pastlife Endowment Rating. Example, Your Crafts 1, Your Pastlife's Crafts 5 with 2 speicalties, and you have a PASTLIFE of 3. 1 + 5 + 2(specialties) - 3(pastlife endowment) = Roll 5 dice. If you Succeed on the roll, you gain a temporary disassociative disorder derangement, as you've drawn to much of your pastlife into your consciousness. You suffer penalties to social interactions, forget who you are, etc. Use the Schizophrenia or MPD rules in the corebook. This lasts for one scene per success rolled.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/509-tiwaztyrsfist","name":"TiwazTyrsfist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar509_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T21:59:01-07:00","id":560374,"title":"","content":"I've been chewing on this idea forever now, and can't shake the idea of a Conspiracy dedicating to fighting Vampires and Mummies, with a focus on the latter. The Arisen lack 'sticky' threats beyond themselves and their fallen kin, the Shuankhsen. Even their 'dedicated' antagonists (like Last Dynasty International, or the Followers of Shulpae) aren't likely to harry them across multiple Descents. Similarly, a loose line of hunters that pursue a dedicated lineage of Kindred seems like a solid bogeyman.<br /> <br /> I like the idea of them being skill monkeys, rather than having any overtly magical gifts; stuff like trading ratings between skills at the cost of a Derangement/Condition for the scene, saving on the unnecessary book-keeping of two full skill lists. Stealing the second and fifth dots of Professional Training (9-again and applying the rote quality) temporarily seems like a simple, elegant mechanic.<br /> <br /> Any thoughts? Sorry for the necro.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T00:15:25-07:00","id":560500,"title":"","content":"Well if you want to make them Mummy specific, make them &quot;survivors&quot; of Irem.<br /> <br /> &quot;You were betrayed, you were sacrificed to create undead abominations to serve their masters until the end of time. They broke death, you awake life after life, your soul cannot rest until the works of Irem fall to dust as they should. You judge the judges.&quot;<br /> <br /> You do have immortals, right? Because there is a brand of immortal who are just serial reincarnates like this concept, so you may want to take a look and see what you like or don't like from them.<br /> <br /> Presuming one uses the rules for research and development in one's game, hunters can get skills up to 8 through endowments. To fit the concept of skill monkey, you should enable this group to do the same thing, or something better.<br /> <br /> For example-<br /> <br /> One wouldn't necessarily have to use new mechanics, one could reskin mentor as, I don't know, personae.<br /> <br /> Mentors have three skills, and an agenda. So each persona could have three skills they can help with, but calling them up has a price- vices, hobbies, goals, etc, that get imposed on the hunter.<br /> <br /> Say for example- Fergus was a hunter in the professional sense, he helps with survival, athletics, and stealth, but Fergus doesn't like modern living, calling upon Fergus causes the hunter to disdain modern trappings- The hunter finds themselves desiring fresh air and the taste of freshly killed meat.<br /> <br /> Clyde was a petty thief living on the street, he can help with Larceny, streetwise, and brawl, but Clyde lived hand to mouth, calling upon Clyde causes the hunter to eat at every opportunity and hoard resources &quot;just in case.&quot;<br /> <br /> Since mentor is only usable once, the key would be to have several personae, but if using the Irem idea the hunters would have 6000 years worth of personae at their disposal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":391,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","user":"StSword","date":". 06-19-2015, 03:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T00:06:28-07:00","id":568884,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure these guys need a direct tie to Irem, especially since they can also hunt Vampires and other immortals just as easily. And now I'm torn between ancestors in one bloodline (which helps codify them, giving a sort of &quot;this is what the family does&quot; element) and far-flung, random past lives (which allows for a greater variety of character concepts, but barely ties them together into a coherent conspiracy).<br /> <br /> I'm currently toying with the idea of each Ancestor having a suite of Skills and Specialties that can be donned for a scene at the cost of a Derangement/Condition (or maybe even a new Breaking Point), but that feels really underpowered for an actual full Endowment. Maybe mimicking the effects of the Praestantia discipline from VtR (dots add to a Skill, failed rolls can be aborted before they're acted upon) in a given skill? I do like the idea of given 9- or 8-again (or maybe even rote action), to make up for the lack of flashy powers.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":281,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","user":"atamajakki","date":". 06-26-2015, 03:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T22:01:14-07:00","id":569957,"title":"","content":"I'd consider reading or asking about Masques from the Guardians of the Veil in Mage, especially in the 2nd edition. Considering Masques are, to my knowledge, alternate personas possibly with alternate skills that the Guardians employ to do dirty work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T23:23:51-07:00","id":569993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/46642-need-help-conceptualizing-an-idea-for-a-conspiracy-the-incarnates?p=569957#post569957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd consider reading or asking about Masques from the Guardians of the Veil in Mage, especially in the 2nd edition. Considering Masques are, to my knowledge, alternate personas possibly with alternate skills that the Guardians employ to do dirty work.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm reading over the 1e book now, and really like what I see; Masques are basically a lower-powered version of what I'm thinking for these guys. Will report back with some more ideas in a few days.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-27T20:19:03-07:00","id":570850,"title":"","content":"Well you certainly don't need to make them tied to Irem, just an idea.<br /> <br /> As for it being a single family limiting things, not really.<br /> <br /> Mitochrondrial Eve might have been up to 200,000 years ago, so if you make the family old enough they could have members on every continent. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-16T11:21:18-08:00","id":831162,"title":"","content":"To revive this after thinking; what if they were folks who accessed their past lives via delving into the deepest parts of their Oneiroi? I'm sure they themselves wouldn't understand it as such, but a discussion about how souls might work in the CofD (especially in light of Mage talk describing Legacies as &quot;shaping the vessel the soul resides in&quot;) inspired me as to the how of this group. Individuals are haunted by dreams of past lives and bizarre deja vu until they eventually gain the mental fortitude to reach the Astral consciously and unlock these memories.<br /> <br /> Mechanically, I'm struggling to differentiate them from the Masques of the Guardians of the Veil. I was thinking something like this: <br /> <br /> For each dot in the Endowment, gain a Specialty and two dots of skills tied to that personality (so four dots in a given personality would have eight Skill dots to assign and four Specialties); they personality can then be accessed with a Willpower point expenditure and a Resolve + Composure roll, with failure still granting the bonus abilities for a scene but adding a Condition to reflect intrusive memories and a feeling of being unmoored in time. You can take the Endowment multiple times, so a given character might have a Babylonian thief at three dots (who's really gifted at Athletics and Subterfuge) and a Teutonic knight at two (with points in Weaponry and Intimidate).<br /> <br /> This still feels weak, but I'm unsure how to pump the power level up without adding in full-on supernatural powers. Thoughts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T04:39:08-08:00","id":831654,"title":"","content":"Two options come to mind. Each past life also comes with 1 dot per level of physical merits - these only manifest when the character is in a spirit world or Twilight of some kind, when they may also physically transform into their past selves.<br /> <br /> Or my preferred option, if they can recall past lives, it makes sense that they might be able to do other superlative tricks with their memories. If they're tied to their Oneiroi, perhaps they have elaborate memory scapes, something like a Beast's Lair containing the events of their past lives - they don't have an Eidetic Memory as such, unless they buy the dots for it, but can find any memory from any of their lives if they can take the time to go exploring (that may also be how they can connect with additional past lives, by finding the routes into them). Of course where there's a realm, there's a chance of someone invading it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T12:19:16-08:00","id":831962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/46642-need-help-conceptualizing-an-idea-for-a-conspiracy-the-incarnates?p=831654#post831654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Two options come to mind. Each past life also comes with 1 dot per level of physical merits - these only manifest when the character is in a spirit world or Twilight of some kind, when they may also physically transform into their past selves.<br /> <br /> Or my preferred option, if they can recall past lives, it makes sense that they might be able to do other superlative tricks with their memories. If they're tied to their Oneiroi, perhaps they have elaborate memory scapes, something like a Beast's Lair containing the events of their past lives - they don't have an Eidetic Memory as such, unless they buy the dots for it, but can find any memory from any of their lives if they can take the time to go exploring (that may also be how they can connect with additional past lives, by finding the routes into them). Of course where there's a realm, there's a chance of someone invading it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps use some of the real-world lore of the akashic records and maybe give thek an ability to enter a &quot;palace of the mind?&quot; I'm trying to consider the implication of physically entering the Astral and how that might reshape the Conspiracy as a whole.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T20:17:59-08:00","id":832294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/46642-need-help-conceptualizing-an-idea-for-a-conspiracy-the-incarnates#post46642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Should they be an organization at a specific point in time that are now coming back together via their descendants, or just people who share this odd ability to recall the skills of past lives and put them to work fighting supernaturals? I feel like I'm missing the meat of my own idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bIf you want an organization then there could be a ritual were mortals swear an oath that carries on even beyond death. If you're just after one special group for this one chronicle then maybe in their past (first) life they were present at some terrible and unnatural event and came to be caught in its wake, perhaps they are reborn whenever it starts up again. As for how they come together you could treat them as a soul circle, souls that are always reincarnated with ties to each other or are inexplicably drawn to each other, with a sense of deja vu recognition when they meet in each life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T23:30:18-08:00","id":832352,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/832338-minor-template-the-incarnates\">It's rough, but functional.</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}